    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44560" root="&#xA;                        وسع&#xA;                    " body-key="w1">
                        
                            2
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَّعَ</span></b> 
                        
                        <i>He made wide, broad, spacious, roomy,</i>
or <i>ample.</i> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَّعَ لَهُ فِى المَجْلِسِ</span>
                        <i>He made room,
or ample space, for him in the sitting-place.</i> (S,
art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسح</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  [And so] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى المَجْلِسِ</span> ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَوَاسَّعُوا</span></b> 
                        <i>They made room, or ample space,</i> [<i>one for
another,</i>] <i>in the sitting-place.</i> (S, art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فسح</span>.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4- 
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَّعَ عَلَيْهِ</span>, for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَسَّعَ عَلَيْهِ رِزْقَهُ</span>, <i>He</i> (God) <i>amplified, enlarged,</i> or <i>made ample</i> or <i>plentiful, his
means of subsistence; contr. of</i>
                        <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَيَّقَ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  See 1,
and 4.

